{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Closing evidence — all 5 AC re-verified on the landed tree\n\nMerged as **`e21f3240cd0`** (Gerrit 3169, patch set 3). Fast-forward, so the landed SHA is\nidentical to the local commit and no post-merge diff comparison was needed.\n\n| AC | Result |\n|---|---|\n| AC1 | `git grep -nE '(^\\|[^A-Za-z0-9_])(_ALIASES\\|_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES\\|_map_legacy_env)([^A-Za-z0-9_]\\|$)' -- src tests scripts ':(exclude)tests/fixtures'` → **0 hits** (baseline 9) |\n| AC2 | `tombstones()` → **6 rows, all `behavior==\"error\"`**, `removed_in` = `v0.8.0`×5 + `v0.12.0`×1, exactly 2 distinct releases (baseline 19 = 6 error + 13 warn) |\n| AC3 | `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py` **18 passed**; `TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR=x rebar list` exits non-zero naming both `v0.8.0` and `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`; `config.py:382-385` intact |\n| AC4 | the 3 named `test_config_backcompat.py` tests **passed** |\n| AC5 | all 3 generator `--check`s exit 0; `ruff check --select C901 src/rebar/_config_sections.py` reports **no `coerce_sparse` finding**; `make verify` green |\n\nAll 5 new tests named in the plan exist: `test_every_tombstone_names_its_real_removal_release`,\n`test_only_error_class_rows_remain`, `test_unknown_llm_key_warns_like_a_core_key`,\n`test_unknown_llm_key_errors_under_strict`, `test_known_llm_key_never_warns`.\nRelease note present in both `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n`make verify` on the landed tree: **20,111 passed / 27 skipped / 0 failures**, 41m21s, exit 0.\n\n## AC3's line citation has drifted — recorded, not edited\n\nAC3 cites `test_error_env_var_fails_loud:124` for the `removed_in in out` assertion. On the\nlanded tree that function is at `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py:139`\nand the assertion is at `:149`:\n\n```python\nassert ri.removed_in in out, f\"error must name the removed-in version {ri.removed_in}\"\n```\n\nThe substance is unchanged — the assertion exists and passes. Recording the drift in a comment\nrather than editing the AC text, because AC text is inside the material hash and an edit would\ninvalidate the certified plan review.\n\n## A defect in my own harness, for the record\n\nMy first AC3 probe grepped a file named `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_error_env_var_fails_loud.py`.\nNo such file exists — the AC names a *function*, not a module. The probe reported `FAIL` for a\ntree that was correct. This is the same wrong-probe class seen on `a018-a2c0-...`'s AC1: a\nprobe that cannot observe the thing it was pointed at returns a confident wrong answer, and the\nflaw is invisible in the verdict alone. Corrected by running the real test file (18 passed).\n\n## Landing was blocked by a merge conflict reported as a stale revision\n\nThe first submit attempt returned Gerrit 409. `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py` printed\n`refusing stale submit: Gerrit reports revision is no longer current`, but Gerrit's detail\nendpoint confirmed the revision *was* current. The real body:\n\n```\nCannot rebase db3f3e396f1...: Change 3169 could not be rebased due to a conflict during merge.\nmerge conflict(s):\n* docs/release-notes.md\n```\n\n`a018-a2c0-...` (`5cd7e2784ab`) and this change both inserted a new section directly beneath the\n`docs/release-notes.md` header. Pre-rebased onto `5cd7e2784ab` per the documented exception,\nkept both sections with this one newest-first, and proved each byte-identical to its source;\nthe non-release-notes diff stayed identical to the pre-rebase commit at 1137 lines, and the\n`Change-Id` was preserved. Patch set 3 then re-earned both votes.\n\nThe misreporting is filed as **`f6b9-8d8e-4f56-4003`** (`tenuous-decorative-chimpanzee`),\nlinked `discovered_from` this ticket.\n\n## Unblocks\n\n`b939-bc68-...` becomes claimable. This change also removes the last `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`\nreference (the `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:177` docstring), which clears\n**AC1 of `25a4-1ab3-3558-4cd4`** — confirmed: 1 hit on `5cd7e2784ab`, 0 on `e21f3240cd0`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793439170926957697,"uuid":"8c50742a-c795-4836-aa8f-c29f02c8371a"}